      "body": "## Motivation\n\nPart of #43147, for the GLM-4.7 / GLM-5 parser.\n\n#43147 reports that `parse_arguments` in `glm4_moe_detector.py` falls back to `ast.literal_eval`, which turns a bare comma into a Python tuple, so a scalar the model wrote as `1,000` reaches the tool as the JSON array `[1, 0]`. #43264 fixes that file.\n\n`glm47_moe_detector.py` (used by `--tool-call-parser glm47` for GLM-4.7 and GLM-5) has its own copy of `parse_arguments` with the same Strategy 3 and the same bug, and #43264 doesn't touch it. On current main:\n\n```\nparse_arguments(\"1,000\", \"number\")   -> ((1, 0), True)\nGlm47MoeDetector, <arg_value>1,000</arg_value> for a number param -> {\"n\": [1, 0]}   (streaming and non-streaming)\n```\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `glm47_moe_detector.py`: when Strategy 3 returns a tuple, fall through to Strategy 4 (keep the raw string), unless the argument is array-typed. Array-typed arguments get the tuple as a list, which is exactly what the client saw before (`json.dumps` already turned the tuple into an array), so `1, 2` for an array param still becomes `[1, 2]`. Only non-array arguments change.\n- `test_glm47_schema_types.py`:\n  - `test_bare_comma_value_is_not_split_into_an_array` runs end to end through `Glm47MoeDetector` with the existing `check_arguments` helper (non-streaming, plus streaming at chunk sizes 1, 7 and full).\n  - `test_parse_arguments_bare_comma` covers the reported inputs and pins the array-typed behaviour.\n\nBoth tests fail on current main and pass with this change. Tests live in the GLM-4.7 test file, so this doesn't overlap with #43264's changes.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nN/A: parser-only change, no change to model forward or kernels.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A.\n\n## Tests run\n\nCPU-only (Python 3.13, torch 2.14.1+cpu, Linux container):\n\n```\npython -m pytest test/registered/unit/function_call/\n631 passed, 1633 subtests passed\n```\n\n`pre-commit run --files <changed files>`: all hooks pass.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to pre-commit.\n- [x] Add unit tests (bug regression; fails on main, passes with the fix).\n- [ ] Update documentation (N/A).\n- [ ] Accuracy/speed benchmarks (N/A, parser-only).\n\nAI assistance: this change was prepared with an AI coding assistant (Claude Code). I reviewed every line and ran the tests above.\n\ncc @JustinTong0323 (function_call code owner)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37877743749](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37877743749)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37877743364](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37877743364)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37877743534](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37877743534)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
