  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "Hi @JustinTong0323, could you add `run-ci` (or `/tag-run-ci-label`) when you get a chance? This and #43275 are small GLM-4.7 tool-parser fixes; lint passes and `tests/registered/unit/function_call` passes locally (631 passed).",
      "created_at": "2026-10-09T15:43:44Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/43270#issuecomment-6084228353",
      "id": 6084228353,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-09T15:43:44Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "Shreyasg13"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Hi @JustinTong0323, could you add the `run-ci` label and review when you have a moment? This stops the GLM-4.7/5 tool parser from splitting comma-containing string values into arrays. It's a companion to #43275 (same detector and test file). Thanks!",
      "created_at": "2026-10-10T19:37:35Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/43270#issuecomment-6101422397",
      "id": 6101422397,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-10T19:37:35Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "Shreyasg13"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "@JustinTong0323 @hnyls2002 bumping this one. It's a silent data-corruption bug: a number argument written as `1,000` reaches the tool as the array `[1, 0]`, both with and without streaming, and nothing raises an error. It's the GLM-4.7/5 half of #43147. #43264 fixes the GLM-4 parser the same way, and git-jxj and I agreed on matching behavior there, so reviewing both together keeps the two parsers consistent. It's one small change plus tests that fail on main. Could you add `run-ci`?\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-14T22:24:35Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/43270#issuecomment-6179853172",
      "id": 6179853172,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-14T22:24:35Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "Shreyasg13"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Gentle ping for review. Both fixes are covered by the added tests (streamed tool arguments are now valid JSON in all 132 cases, previously 36 failed). I can rebase on main if anything has moved. Could a maintainer add the run-ci label so CI can run? Thanks!",
      "created_at": "2026-10-17T04:14:34Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/43270#issuecomment-6229513293",
      "id": 6229513293,
